00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:32.180
example of something that really surprised
me you know i always feel like most of my

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:40.200
leaps in writing quality come from writing
something else you know so for example many

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:47.660
many long time ago i was uh i had a i was
writing a screenplay and i had a book that

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:50.870
i was reading about writing novels because
i was always trying to write a novel you know

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:55.110
sort of in the background of everything and
i don't even think this was a particularly

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:59.650
good book about writing novels but it had
one tip that i think is gold like this is

00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:03.620
a million dollar tip so for anyone who's watching
this i guarantee you this will improve your

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:11.260
writing and it's the tip was when you're finished
with a manuscript do a word search for ly

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:17.600
because most adverbs end in l y and adverbs
are usually imprecise and are not the best

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:21.380
word for what you're trying to convey and
i was like wow like that really stood out

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:25.640
to me and so i took my script that i was working
on i'll try it on my script and i tried it

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:29.340
on my script and sure enough when i finished
i was like this is better you know like it

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:35.159
really made it better so i mean i think i
think a lot of times when you're writing you

00:01:35.159 --> 00:01:38.490
know your first draft you're kind of just
trying to get it down but if you can go back

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:42.650
and say what was i really trying to say there
you know and if you're using words like he

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:48.400
walked slowly to the door like well is that
really what you mean or do you mean he stalked

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:52.870
towards the door or he crept towards the door
you know or he sneaked towards the door and

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:57.280
you know if you know i don't think always
that applies but a lot of times i think you'll

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:01.730
find that you were really trying to say something
else a little more specific and by getting

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:06.800
rid of that adverb and finding the the right
word it's going to make the scene pop you

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:10.399
know in the reader's head it makes it much
more visual because you can envision someone

00:02:10.399 --> 00:02:15.620
sneaking but if you envision someone walking
slowly you might not see the same thing you

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:19.350
know and i think that really helped my writing
oh that was just one of those little like

